# Stage 4's promotion list for the cbp2025 host: 16 traces.
#
# After the search, the few best candidates are scored again here, together
# with the kit's default host and the port at the paper's defaults. The
# search picked its winners on a screening list, and a winner on a few traces
# can lose on others. This list is the check on that.
#
# Why not all 105. training-105.list takes about 3.5 hours per candidate on
# this cluster's 4 trace slots, and promotion scores 3 finalists plus two
# comparison runs. This list takes about 30 minutes per candidate, estimated
# from the ExecTime column of the kit's reference_results_training_set.csv,
# which matched the ~8 minutes measured for perf-4.list.
#
# How the traces were chosen, so the choice can be repeated or audited:
# - None is in perf-8.list or screening-60.list. The search never saw them.
# - The six families keep roughly their shares of the 105:
#   int 5, web 4, infra 2, fp 2, compress 2, media 1.
# - Within a family, the pick is random.Random(20260923).sample over the
#   remaining traces sorted by name, families in the order above.
# - Three traces over 800 s were left out first: compress_7 (1377 s),
#   int_32 (992 s) and int_33 (821 s). Any one of them alone would set the
#   finish time of the whole list.
#
# Sixteen traces is still a small sample. Report how many traces improved,
# not only the mean, because one unusual trace can move a mean this small.
int/int_25_trace.gz
int/int_26_trace.gz
int/int_27_trace.gz
int/int_35_trace.gz
int/int_36_trace.gz
web/web_15_trace.gz
web/web_18_trace.gz
web/web_22_trace.gz
web/web_23_trace.gz
infra/infra_9_trace.gz
infra/infra_15_trace.gz
fp/fp_10_trace.gz
fp/fp_11_trace.gz
compress/compress_5_trace.gz
compress/compress_6_trace.gz
media/media_2_trace.gz
